# Thai date display

When showing dates to users in GoldenSoft HR (and related suite UIs), use **Thai Buddhist-era** format — not ISO and not Gregorian CE in the UI.

## Rules

- **Display**: `DD/MM/BBBB` (พ.ศ.), e.g. `18/06/2569`
- **Ranges**: `01/06/2569 – 30/06/2569`
- **Storage / API**: keep ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` (ค.ศ.)
- **Form fields** for วันเริ่ม / วันสิ้นสุด / hire dates: use `ThaiDateInput` (not bare `<input type="date">`)
- **Do not** show raw `2026-06-18` or Gregorian year alone in user-facing copy

## How to implement (HR)

```ts
import { formatThaiDate, formatThaiDateRange, toIsoDate } from "@/lib/hr/thai-date";
import ThaiDateInput from "@/components/hr/thai-date-input";

formatThaiDate(row.workDate); // "18/06/2569"
<ThaiDateInput value={iso} onChange={setIso} /> // shows วว/ดด/พ.ศ.
```

## Checklist for new UI

- [ ] Tables / headings / messages use Thai helpers
- [ ] Start/end date fields use `ThaiDateInput`
- [ ] Auto-generated names that include dates use Thai format
